Stop recording video for tests that pass, and use the whole runner

The smoke workflow takes about six minutes and **329 seconds of it is one
step**. Everything else is noise: Ruby setup 5s, the Jekyll build 1s, all
seven Python test steps together under 10s. The Playwright suite is the run.

Two changes in `tests/playwright.config.js`. Neither touches a test, and no
coverage is lost.

## `video: 'retain-on-failure'` → `'on-first-retry'`

The setting does not mean what it reads like. It cannot record only failures,
because nothing knows a test will fail until it has — so it records **every**
test start to finish and deletes the file when the test passes. The cost is
paid on the ninety-nine that pass, for the one that does not.

`retries: 1` was already set, so a failing test runs a second time, and that
second run is the one you would actually watch. Recording only there keeps the
diagnosis and stops paying for it on every green run.

Trace and screenshot are untouched — both are genuinely failure-only.

## `workers: '100%'` in CI

`fullyParallel: true` was set, but Playwright defaults to half the machine's
cores. A standard GitHub runner has four, so the suite was running two at a
time. Locally it stays `undefined` — saturating a laptop that is also running
an editor is not a kindness.

## What I did not do

**I left the two projects alone.** Every test runs twice, once as Desktop
Chrome and once as a Pixel 5, and dropping `mobile` from pull requests would
roughly halve the time again.

It is the obvious next cut and I think it is the wrong one. This site is read
on phones — class mode, check-in, the reserve flow — and mobile-only breakage
is exactly what a desktop-only PR gate stops catching. That is a coverage
decision rather than a performance one, so it should be made deliberately and
by you, not folded into a speed change.

If the run is still too slow after this, say so and we can look at it as a
tradeoff with its own argument.

## Verified

Config loaded with a stubbed `@playwright/test` and the resolved values
printed, under CI and not:

| | CI | local |
|---|---|---|
| `workers` | `"100%"` | default |
| `video` | `on-first-retry` | `on-first-retry` |
| `retries` | 1 | 0 |
| projects | desktop, mobile | desktop, mobile |

`trace: retain-on-failure` and `screenshot: only-on-failure` unchanged.

The real measurement is the next run of this workflow, which happens on this
pull request. Compare it against the 329s step.
